Original commit body from a47fd62:

Previously hot spots were ranked by raw test count, which biased toward
larger functions. Now ranks by test density (tests per LOC), surfacing
small utility functions that are disproportionately tested.

Example: A 3-line function with 172 tests (57.33 t/LOC) now correctly
ranks above a 224-line function with 230 tests (1.03 t/LOC).
